<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-806] Parquet-tools silently suppresses error messages</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-806</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Without -debug parameter, parquet-tools produces quite cryptic output in case of errors. For example, parquet tools may print the following output and nothing more:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;org/apache/hadoop/conf/Configuration&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is not clear from this output that it indicates an error (actually it is not clear what it indicates at all). I don&apos;t really understand the reasoning behind hiding exceptions by default, but instead of this unusable message, parquet-tools should at least print:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NoClassDefFoundError: org/apache/hadoop/conf/Configuration&lt;/p&gt;</description>
